  "title": "2026-09-08-reflow-152600 · eval-harness-orchestration",
  "description": "# Offline evaluation harness orchestration\nRead down the execution region, up through grading, then down through comparison. Blue paths retain run material and maintain the baseline.\n\n- A pinned suite freezes scenario definitions and the tested revision, configuration, prompt versions and rubric versions. Wording changes create new scenario versions rather than overwriting history.\n- The scheduler fans out to a bounded worker pool running ordered steps against an isolated SUT, never production. Infrastructure faults are logged and retried; success and product-behavior failures are recorded before continuation. Transcripts, final artifacts and fault types are retained distinctly.\n- Each completed scenario immediately enters globally limited concurrent grading. Independent criteria graders and an artifact-only grader produce verdicts with evidence; the artifact-only grader receives no original request. Missing evidence invalidates a verdict, triggers one retry, and is flagged and excluded if still invalid. Every verdict is archived, including invalid ones.\n- The assembler merges valid verdicts into a scorecard. Comparison with the chosen baseline requires identical fingerprints; incompatible runs are not compared. Compatible score movements at or above the defined threshold are narrated. Promotion sets the future baseline for compatible runs.\n- The run archive retains transcripts, artifacts and verdicts for re-examining disputed scores.",
